            <ArticleTitle>Metastasis of malignant struma ovarii to the lumbar spine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jocn.2009.04.024</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 32-year-old woman with a solitary metastasis to the lumbar spine from a struma ovarii was treated surgically with tumour extirpation and anterior spinal reconstruction. Metastasis may occur when a patient has had prior surgery to remove this rare tumour.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2009 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
